WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
[ YouTube Learning ]

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.440
Now you know how to ask students a single question,

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.840
or how to give them long form assignments

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.280
using Google Classroom.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.360
It’s also easy to create Quiz Assignments

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.360
which have many questions in them!

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.000
And the best part is that you don’t have to grade them.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.820
Google Classroom does it for you!

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:25.120
[ Don't Memorise intro music ]

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:26.620
Pick the class in which

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.620
you want to add the Quiz Assignment.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.060
Go to ClassWork, click on create,

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.440
and then select Quiz Assignment.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.579
Did you notice something?

00:00:36.579 --> 00:00:40.660
Google Classroom automatically created a Google
form for you.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.250
Wait, what’s that?

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.500
Google Forms is a tool that helps you measure student

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.720
progress, administer tests and much more!

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.100
You will see how easy this tool is for creating quizzes!

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.000
Okay back to our original screen.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.400
Give your quiz assignment a title,

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.820
and an appropriate description.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.600
If it’s a graded quiz,

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.200
it will be a good idea

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.600
to keep the Grade Importing option on…

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.820
Here, the word ‘grade’ means

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.820
the Test Scores of your students….

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.000
and then you can

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.520
open the Google Form by clicking here.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:15.200
This is the Screen you will see now!

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.540
You can name your quiz by editing this section!

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.840
You can then tell your students what this quiz is

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:24.320
all about using the description box here.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.200
To make it a little more lively,

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.680
you can click here

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.360
to add a theme or an image to your quiz...

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:32.340
The first question box is

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.520
generated by Google Forms by default.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.780
To add your second question, you simply have to

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.080
click on the PLUS icon you see here!

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:41.940
Now you are ready to post your

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.140
first question of this Quiz!

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.120
The beauty about Google Forms is that it gives

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.080
you a choice to ask many different types of questions!

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.800
It could be a short answer question,

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.800
or a long answer question or

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:57.000
even a Multiple Choice question maybe!

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.280
Let’s pick Multiple Choice for now!

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.840
Let me add a sample question with 4 answer choices

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.260
Once you have entered your question,

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.300
you should also add an Answer Key.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.040
You should mention the correct answer here,

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.080
and assign points to this question.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.260
So if the student answers this correctly,

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.260
she will get 2 points.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:22.000
The ‘Answer Feedback’ button is important as well.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.840
Clicking on it allows you to enter the feedback required

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.060
for students depending on their answer.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.180
If they answer incorrectly,

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.180
we could write something like this,

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.880
and give a video link for reference.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.160
And for correct answers,

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.380
we could give feedback like this.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.920
And then you click on Save.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.280
If you want to make it mandatory for the student

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:45.740
to attempt a question, change this to ‘Required’.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.520
This will not allow the student to go ahead and

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:52.640
submit the quiz unless she has answered this one.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:55.140
You could also add images to your question

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.540
or answer options by clicking here!

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.460
Now let me add another question here

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.460
by clicking on the PLUS icon.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.220
Well, what if you want to see the handwritten

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.200
detailed answers that your students have written?

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.140
Here’s the question.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:12.600
In that case, we can select the “File Upload” option here

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.360
and click on Continue.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:15.840
These are the different file types

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.840
your students can upload.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:20.280
So your students can write detailed answers

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.540
maybe in their notebook and click pictures

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.660
and upload images.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.000
Or if the answer runs into pages,

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.320
they can also upload a pdf file.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:32.200
If some student is finding it difficult to write

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.760
because of an injury, she can also upload

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:38.000
an audio file by narrating the answer.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:41.280
As you can see, there are plenty of options here.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.740
Interesting isn’t it?

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.380
You could add as many questions as you like,

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:47.760
and your quiz will keep getting auto-saved.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:50.240
If you wish to see how students are going

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.520
to see your quiz, you can use the preview

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.400
option right here!

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.360
What if you want your students to attempt

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:59.240
your quiz a maximum of just one time?

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.180
Well, you have that option too.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.340
You just need to go to the Settings section

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.100
and click on Limit to one response.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:11.600
In the middle, we see the presentation section here.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.820
You can also choose to show your students

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:17.040
a progress bar which tells them how many questions

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:20.240
they have answered and how many are left.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.080
Your quiz is now ready.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:25.810
You may close this tab, and come back to this page.

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:27.580
You could also refresh the page once

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.580
for your changes to take effect.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.280
You will see your quiz assignment here

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.300
on your dashboard now!

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.960
Clicking on edit will open the quiz assignment again.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.220
Here you can make it a part of a topic.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:43.660
And then you can assign or schedule for a later date!

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.100
Your students now will be able to see your quiz

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:49.200
in that particular topic of your class!

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.140
And once your students have attempted the quiz,

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.260
you will see all the responses in the

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:56.440
Grades section here.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:59.180
Let’s click on the Quiz Assignment here.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:02.160
We can see that all 9 students of your class

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.020
have turned the assignment in,

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.700
which means they have submitted it.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:07.460
To get the scores,

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:10.420
we just have to click on ‘Import Grades’ here.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.960
And then we can see the scores of the students

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.240
on the left.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:16.780
Clearly, Google Classroom did the job

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:18.940
of automatically grading them.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:21.300
It does save you a lot of time as

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.300
no manual checks are required.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:26.140
You'd have to manually check only the

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:30.200
detailed or subjective answers written by your students!

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:33.360
Google Forms is one of the easiest tools to use

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.040
for quizzes and assessments ,

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.000
and believe me here.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.820
If you spend just 2 focussed hours on it,

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:42.760
you will understand almost 80% of it.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:46.080
So don’t let anything hold you back!

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.000
Happy teaching!

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:55.400
[ #TeachFromAnywhere ]

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.120
[ YouTube Learning ]

